full_article:
A Duquesne University faculty member was killed in the devastating floods and mudslides along the Nepal-China border.

In a letter shared with Channel 11 on Saturday, Duquesne University President David Dausey announced the death of Mark Cantrell of the John G. Rangos Sr. School of Health Sciences.

Cantrell's career reportedly brought him around the globe, working to improve health care access for various populations.

